  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "The average age of \\(33\\) fifth-graders is \\(11.\\) The average age of \\(55\\) of their parents is \\(33.\\) What is the average age of all of these parents and fifth-graders?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(22\\)",
    "B": "\\(23.25\\)",
    "C": "\\(24.75\\)",
    "D": "\\(26.25\\)",
    "E": "\\(28\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "To combine the groups, first recover their total ages by multiplying each average by its group size. The fifth-graders' ages total \\(33\\cdot11=363\\) years, and the parents' ages total \\(55\\cdot33=1815\\) years.\n\nThere are \\(33+55=88\\) people altogether, so their average age is\n\\[\n\\frac{363+1815}{88}\n=\\frac{2178}{88}\n=24.75\n\\]\nyears, choice C.",
